\t\t</td>\n\t\t</tr></tbody></table>","plainText":"REQUIREMENTS FOR DWELLING UNITS District Requirement Waiver Column A Column B Column C Parking requirement per standard dwelling unit (in percent) Parking requirement per dwelling unit that is an ancillary dwelling unit, qualifying senior housing or an income-restricted unit in qualifying affordable housing (in percent) Maximum waiver (in spaces)1, 2 R1 R2 100 0 0 R3-1 R3A R3X R4-1 R4A R4B R5A 50 0 03 R3-2 R4 35 0 5 R5 35 0 10 R5B R5D 25 0 10 R6 R7-1 R7-2 25 0 15 R7A R7B 15 0 15 R7-3 R7D R7X 15 0 25 R8 12 0 30 R9 12 0 40 R10 12 0 50 R11 12 0 60 R12 12 0 75"},{"id":"zr-22799-block-004","kind":"html","html":"<p><sup data-indent-level=\"1\" style=\"margin-left: 40px;\">1 &nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;For <strong><em>qualifying residential sites</em></strong> in R1 through R5 Districts, <strong><em>accessory</em></strong> off-street parking spaces shall be waived where the number of <strong><em>dwelling units</em></strong> is 75 or less.&nbsp;</sup></p>","plainText":"1 For qualifying residential sites in R1 through R5 Districts, accessory off-street parking spaces shall be waived where the number of dwelling units is 75 or less."},{"id":"zr-22799-block-005","kind":"html","html":"<p><sup data-indent-level=\"1\" style=\"margin-left: 40px;\">2 &nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;For <strong><em>zoning lots</em></strong> in R7-2, R7-3, R8, R9, R10, R11 or R12 Districts, the parking requirements shall be waived where the <strong><em>lot area</em></strong> is 10,000 square feet or less.&nbsp;</sup></p>","plainText":"2 For zoning lots in R7-2, R7-3, R8, R9, R10, R11 or R12 Districts, the parking requirements shall be waived where the lot area is 10,000 square feet or less."},{"id":"zr-22799-block-006","kind":"html","html":"<p><sup data-indent-level=\"1\" style=\"margin-left: 40px;\">3 &nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;For <strong><em>zoning lots</em></strong> existing on December 5, 2024 where the <strong><em>lot width</em></strong> is 25 feet or less, no parking shall be required. In addition, irrespective of the <strong><em>lot width</em></strong> of the <strong><em>zoning lot</em></strong>, in R4B Districts, one <strong><em>accessory</em></strong> off-street parking space may be waived.</sup></p>","plainText":"3 For zoning lots existing on December 5, 2024 where the lot width is 25 feet or less, no parking shall be required. In addition, irrespective of the lot width of the zoning lot, in R4B Districts, one accessory off-street parking space may be waived."},{"id":"zr-22799-block-007","kind":"html","html":"<p>No spaces shall be required on any <strong><em>zoning lot</em></strong> where there is no way to arrange the required spaces with access to the <strong><em>street</em></strong> to conform to the provisions of Section <a class=\"sec-link-inline\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-5#25-63\" data-permitext-zr-source=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-5#25-63\"><span>25-63</span></a> (Location of Access to the Street).<br>\n&nbsp;</p>","plainText":"No spaces shall be required on any zoning lot where there is no way to arrange the required spaces with access to the street to conform to the provisions of Section 25-63 (Location of Access to the Street)."}],"zoning":{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceNodeID":22799,"sourcePath":"/article-ii/chapter-5/25-222","sourceURL":"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-5/25-222","sourceContentHash":"2299918fe1bfe384a2e1397cfb969ddbcee5a9214982ef40a831f13ccd55fbb6","article":{"roman":"II","title":"Residence District Regulations"},"chapter":{"number":"5","title":"Accessory Off-Street Parking and Loading Regulations","canonicalNumber":"II-5"},"appendix":null,"subsections":[],"tables":[{"id":"zr-22799-table-001","ordinal":0,"sourceAnchor":null,"caption":null,"plainText":"REQUIREMENTS FOR DWELLING UNITS District Requirement Waiver Column A Column B Column C Parking requirement per standard dwelling unit (in percent) Parking requirement per dwelling unit that is an ancillary dwelling unit, qualifying senior housing or an income-restricted unit in qualifying affordable housing (in percent) Maximum waiver (in spaces)1, 2 R1 R2 100 0 0 R3-1 R3A R3X R4-1 R4A R4B R5A 50 0 03 R3-2 R4 35 0 5 R5 35 0 10 R5B R5D 25 0 10 R6 R7-1 R7-2 25 0 15 R7A R7B 15 0 15 R7-3 R7D R7X 15 0 25 R8 12 0 30 R9 12 0 40 R10 12 0 50 R11 12 0 60 R12 12 0 75","contentHash":"4f2cd227a71693de0b5ec391c258fa12d8390b222f1544b47f4e9341a222f93b"}],"mapReferences":[],"appendixReferences":[],"specialDistrict":null,"amendmentHistory":[{"effectiveDate":"2024-12-05","reportNumber":"N240290ZRY","reportURL":"http://a030-cpc.nyc.gov/html/cpc/report.aspx?num=N%20240290%20ZRY","projectName":"City of Yes for Housing Opportunity","action":"Added","notes":null,"description":"An amendment modifying multiple Sections to expand opportunities for housing within all zoning districts, and across all 59 of the City’s Community Districts"}],"amendmentHistorySourceURL":"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/ajax/get/amendment/section/22799","effectiveDate":"2024-12-05","lastAmended":"2024-12-05","version":"NYC Zoning Resolution — text through 2026-08-13","researchEligibility":false}}
